Subject: [PATCH 4/9] EXEC-MU-ACCOUNTS ultracode re-check C-P2 (Phase 2
 entitlements): failing tests of verified findings

- test_c_p2_recheck.py: Principal.refusal gives CAPABILITY_REQUIRED, never PLAN_EXPIRED, for the list and limit
  restrictions (terminal.tickers, terminal.history_days) that Phase 3c refuses through p.refusal; RESTRICTIVE's list is
  one shared object handed to every principal with a malformed list; seed_subscription counts a '*' = false row as
  holding every capability.
- test_c_p2_terminal_wire_domain.py: values Phase 2 accepts or produces (history_days 0 or above 36600, tickers outside
  ^[A-Z0-9]{1,12}$, the RESTRICTIVE 0) make terminal-api refuse the 3c x-terminal-capabilities header 400 for every
  Terminal call; skips until Phase 3c's terminal_access.py is in the tree (6 failures on p3c-int 7f95aff9).

